issue.body:
Jira Link: [DB-2643](https://yugabyte.atlassian.net/browse/DB-2643)
### Description

Range-partitioned colocated index reverse scan _after TRUNCATE_ fails with DocDB error `Cannot decode value type kGroupEnd from the key encoding format: "!"` (see issues with same message: #10279, #12422).  The truncate is necessary to reproduce.  Repro on recent master commits 25ce96c6bbe8bec5036f95f687e3f5672a12b044 and b661d0a0a71302b3c57097db402f90a6ae11b938:

```sql
CREATE TABLEGROUP g;
CREATE TABLE t (i int) TABLEGROUP g;
CREATE INDEX ON t (i);
TRUNCATE t;
INSERT INTO t VALUES (1), (2), (3);
EXPLAIN SELECT i FROM t WHERE i = 2;
SELECT i FROM t WHERE i = 2;
EXPLAIN SELECT i FROM t WHERE i > 1;
SELECT i FROM t WHERE i > 1;
EXPLAIN SELECT i FROM t WHERE i < 3;
SELECT i FROM t WHERE i < 3;
```

```
ERROR:  Query error: Cannot decode value type kGroupEnd from the key encoding format: "!"
```

For colocated index, default partitioning is ASC.  If the index is specified DESC (i.e. `CREATE INDEX ON t (i DESC)`), the `i > 1` query fails instead of `i < 3`.

Recently, having index separated from table was disallowed (commit 307cf89ab91b50ae060ffb798a1c5835db660b43).  Reverting that restriction, this still fails when table is not colocated but index is.

I noticed that the table tombstone created by colocated truncate still exists after `yb-admin compact_table` for both the table and index.  That is strange when related tests in `src/yb/docdb/docdb-test.cc` pass.  See also related issue #12898.
